Subject: Do not shmdt() a segment that shmop_open() never attached
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

When shmop_open() fails before or at shmat(), it releases the Shmop object
with addr still NULL or (char *) -1, and the free handler passed that to
shmdt(). Glibc returns EINVAL; Fil-C's shmdt wrapper rejects the pointer and
stops the process, so every shmop_open() error killed PHP.

--- a/ext/shmop/shmop.c
+++ b/ext/shmop/shmop.c
@@ -99,7 +99,11 @@ static void shmop_free_obj(zend_object *object)
 {
 	php_shmop *shmop = shmop_from_obj(object);
 
-	shmdt(shmop->addr);
+	/* shmop_open() releases the object when it fails before or at shmat(),
+	 * leaving addr NULL or (char *) -1. */
+	if (shmop->addr && shmop->addr != (char *) -1) {
+		shmdt(shmop->addr);
+	}
 
 	zend_object_std_dtor(&shmop->std);
 }
